  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The three legal tests",
      "items": [
        "The covered product must not be linked to deforestation after 31 Dec 2020.",
        "It must be produced in line with relevant laws in its country of production.",
        "For wood, the rule also covers forest degradation after that date."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What evidence means",
      "items": [
        "Identify the production country, production period, suppliers and product.",
        "Provide geolocation for every production plot; for cattle, identify the holdings.",
        "Keep verifiable evidence supporting both deforestation-free status and legality."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Who is responsible?",
      "items": [
        "The operator remains responsible, including when relying on an existing statement.",
        "Non-SME traders generally have operator-like due-diligence duties.",
        "SME traders must keep supplier, buyer and statement-reference records."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Checks and consequences",
      "items": [
        "Authorities select checks using risk; customs also checks relevant import / export references.",
        "If goods are non-compliant, they can be stopped or withdrawn; authorities can require corrective action and apply penalties."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Scope and reading note",
      "items": [
        "The rule covers seven commodities and only the derived goods specifically listed in Annex I—not every product that uses them.",
        "This overview follows the Regulation (EU) 2023/1115 text provided in eudr.txt. It is an orientation aid, not legal advice; check the current consolidated rules for a real transaction."
      ]
    }
